question_description:
// Write a function that gives the first common manager for 2 employees.
// You may design the data structure and APIs as you see fit.
//
// Examples:
// Michael and Timothy -> Ann
// Sofia and Isabel -> Jeff
//
//

                Jeff
                 +
                 |
       +---------+--------+--------+
       |         |        |        |
       +         +        +        +
     Ann      Mathew   Jessica   George
      +                           +
      |                           |
   +-------+                 +--------+
   |       |                 |        |      
   +       +                 +        +      
Timothy  Sofia            Andrew    Isabel  
	         +
	         |
	     +---+---+
	     |       |
	             +
	         Michael

//
// Find the first common manager
// Input: two person's name, Two nodes are given.
// Output : the node of lowest manager.
This question is similar to Leetcode 1650, but you need to design the data structure instead of having the definition of the tree node.

Assuming there is a data set that contains UPC, Date and Price. Knowing many UPCs may map to a single ASIN, calculate the average price per ASIN per month.
Clarification with the interviewer:
// UPC means: ID string
// Date means: time
// ASIN means: Amazon Standard Identification Number. It’s a unique 10-character alphanumeric code assigned to every product listed in the Amazon store.
// UPCs => ASIN many to one
// One ASIN can have many UPCs associated, each UPC has a price.
// Per month added
One UPC contains information like this: this can be an array of UPCs given to us.
UPC Date Price
// UPC1, 10/12/10, $1
// UPC1, 10/13/10, $2
// UPC1, 10/13/10, $1
// UPC2342, 10/13/10, $7
UPCs can map to different ASINs as below: this can be a map given to us showing the relation between UPC and ASIN.
// UPC1 -> ASIN1
// UPC2342 -> ASIN2

The IT team at Amazon has device configurations for Amazon employees' devices for their work laptops, work mobile phones, etc.
Assuming there's a RemoteConfigurationSender service implemented that sends the given configuration to the device, write the LLD for the device configurations manager.
Device configurations can be like:
{
  "namespace": "com.amazon.laptop",
  "attributes": {
    "key1": "value1",
    "key2": "value2",
  },
  "priority": 1
}

Implement an interface to track asset usage:
interface UsageTracker {    
   void recordUsage(Integer assetId);
   void decrementUsage(Integer assetId);
   Integer getMostUsed();
}
Example usage:
usageTracker.recordUsage(101);
usageTracker.recordUsage(102);
usageTracker.getMostUsed(); // Result: 101 or 102 (Tie)
usageTracker.recordUsage(101);
usageTracker.getMostUsed(); // Result: 101
usageTracker.recordUsage(102); 
usageTracker.recordUsage(102);
usageTracker.getMostUsed(); // Result: 102
usageTracker.decrementUsage(102);
usageTracker.decrementUsage(102);
usageTracker.getMostUsed(); // Result: 101 (since 101 has count 2)
usageTracker.decrementUsage(101);
usageTracker.decrementUsage(101);
usageTracker.decrementUsage(102);
usageTracker.getMostUsed(); // Result: -1 (All usage records cleared)
